  "findings": "Chosen false Solomon seal replacement for the explicitly temperate-listed generic tall woodland bloom placeholder; legacy ID retained, not identification of the former jungle asset. Compared terminal branched cream-white spring plumes and alternate broad leaves in three NCSU-hosted photographs with current seeds 1, 4 and 7 plus all 36 current variants. Added alternate leaves on leaning curved shoots and branched terminal inflorescences; replaced the inherited autumn-orange head with the existing white material token. Increased spread to separate shoots and prevent the narrow tower habit of the first pilot. Sizes span roughly 0.4-0.85 m. Individual millimetre florets and leaf veins are unresolved at 25 mm; small terminal panicles reduce to a few white cells. Accepted as a stylized spring clump with no autumn berries.",
